Open Source Evolution License (OSEL)
Version 0.1 — Working Draft
=====================================

The Open Source Evolution License (OSEL) is a draft open source license
that permits a recipient, when distributing a new version of the software,
to evolve the license into a stricter OSI-approved compatible license.

This repository contains the official specification, drafting notes,
compliance analysis, and supporting documentation for OSEL.

Status
------

OSEL Version 0.1 is a working draft.

It has not been submitted to the Open Source Initiative (OSI) for
certification. It is not an OSI-approved license. Do not describe it as
"OSI Approved" or "OSI Certified".

The name "Open Source Evolution License" and the abbreviation "OSEL" are
used here for identification of this draft. Before adopting the license in
a production project, you should review the text carefully and consider
whether it meets your needs.

What OSEL Does
--------------

OSEL grants the usual open source freedoms: use, reproduction,
modification, distribution, and sublicensing. It also includes:

1. A patent grant from contributors and copyright holders.

2. A patent retaliation termination clause.

3. A contributor grant that covers submitted contributions.

4. A license replacement right under Section 5.

The replacement right allows a recipient, when distributing a new version,
to replace OSEL with a "Compatible License" as defined in Section 1.7.
A Compatible License must be an OSI-approved license that imposes a
strictly greater set of obligations than OSEL. The additional obligations
must fall within the categories listed in Section 1.7(c).

The replacement right is not automatic. It is exercised only upon
distribution of a new version, and only if the conditions in Section 5.1
are met. The original license remains available as an option. A recipient
may always distribute derivative works under OSEL itself.

